{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# HANDOFF STATE — 2026-09-06 ~06:00 UTC\n\nNothing is mid-mutation. No gate op was left half-applied. No `--force` was used anywhere.\n\n## Agents still running (all SAFE to leave; none mutates production unprompted)\n\n1. **r7g.large resize** — in PHASE 1 only: edits `infra/terraform/variables.tf`, runs\n   `terraform plan`, pushes to Gerrit for review. It is explicitly instructed **not to apply** and\n   to wait for an operator go-ahead before Phase 2. Approved cost ceiling is `r7g.large`\n   ($78.18/mo vs $49.06 today); `c7g.xlarge` (+35%) and `m7g.xlarge` (+52%) are OUT.\n2. **memory-bounding (`cryptozoic-unlit-ladybug`)** — running `make verify`; nothing committed or\n   pushed until green. Will report a captured exit code, not the notification's.\n3. **`lousy-unsuited-gnu`** — its change 2723 is MERGED; the agent has not yet filed its final\n   report, which holds the AC evidence.\n\n## Tickets closeable, with their exact remaining step\n\n| ticket | state | next step |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ambitious-creative-ovenbird` (009f) | ACs ticked, file_impact widened 3->4 | attestation staled BY DESIGN -> `rebar review-plan`, then close |\n| `lousy-unsuited-gnu` (94c5) | file_impact complete (2/2), 5 ACs unticked | wait for its agent's report, tick on that evidence, close |\n| `prelawful-lumpish-clingfish` (3ce7) | **file_impact EMPTY** but commit touched 2 files; **no checkbox ACs at all** | set file_impact (`src/rebar/_commands/init.py`, `tests/unit/test_init_leaves_no_detached_upkeep.py`), add ACs, review, close |\n\n## Close-gate rules learned the expensive way — check ALL of these BEFORE the first close attempt\n\ndcc3 took five review passes because I discovered these one at a time:\n\n1. Every `[non-codebase]` AC ticked `[x]` needs an indented `provenance:` line\n   (environment / principal / privilege_posture / instrument).\n2. A `[non-codebase]` AC must NOT cite a repo path — that is **attestation laundering**; split it,\n   keeping the repo-verifiable half UNTAGGED.\n3. Description must be **< 8000 chars** (P4 blocks, it is not advisory).\n4. Heading must be literally `## Acceptance Criteria`.\n5. `file_impact` must cover EVERY file in the merged commit.\n6. Ticking a checkbox is attestation-SAFE; changing AC **text** or `file_impact` is MATERIAL and\n   stales the attestation.\n\n## Operator decisions outstanding\n\n1. **Sizing** — approved at `r7g.large`, Phase 2 apply awaits go-ahead after the change merges.\n   Expect a ~3-minute Gerrit outage (stop/start). Verify afterwards that gate-scratch is still\n   mounted and that **review-bot came back** (it uses `unless-stopped` and did NOT restart after\n   tonight's reboot, silently killing the LLM-Review vote source for 59 minutes).\n2. **Jira bridge** — still DISABLED. 387/389 duplicates closed and independently verified;\n   re-enable checklist is on `decrepit-blowy-javalina`.\n3. **Rotate `JIRA_API_TOKEN`** — an agent expanded it into a transcript. No external transmission.\n\n## Environment at handoff\n\nRoot 29% - memory 58% - load 0.74 - alarms 4 (0 INSUFFICIENT_DATA) - Gerrit HTTP 200 in 0.27s -\nall four containers healthy - MCP on current main - all four reaper timers active.\nThe 4 remaining alarms are the two `var_tmp` + two `container` metrics, blocked on change **2722**\nlanding AND autodeploy re-materialising the probe. After that they should read **1**, not `-1`;\na `-1` would mean the installer half did not take."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788669696992615001,"uuid":"a9877d3e-2135-4ed0-a1ab-a7d3bc8e6053"}